: \nL64: cite24†How you can get more involved L65: cite25†Get brochures, posters and forms L66: \nL67: cite26†Download resources L68: \nL69: cite27†Candidate Hub L70: \nL71: cite28†Election Access Fund L72: \nL73: cite29†Community Education Fund L74: \nL75:   * Stats and research Ngā tatauranga me te rangahau\nL76: \nL77: cite30†Enrolment statistics L78: \nL79: cite31†Participation in voting L80: \nL81: cite32†Applications for roll data L82: \nL83: cite33†MMP seat allocation calculator L84: \nL85: cite34†Party donations and loans L86: \nL87: cite35†Election reports L88: \nL89: cite36†Election results†electionresults.govt.nz L90: \nL91: cite5†About us cite6†Media & news cite7†Jobs†work.elections.nz cite8†Contact L92: cite37†Party Portal Login L93: \nL94: [Button: In this section]\nL95: \nL96: cite15†Candidate Hub L97: \nL98:   * cite38†Becoming a candidate L99:     * cite39†How to become a candidate L100:     * Becoming a candidate in the 2026 General Election\nL101:     * cite40†Election Access Fund L102:   * cite41†Key information and dates L103:   * cite42†Candidate rules L104:   * cite43†Resources L105: \nL106: Candidate nominations for the general election open on Monday 7 September 2026.\nL107: ### Individual electorate candidate nominations\nL108: \nL109: The individual nomination form must be completed by:\nL110: \nL111:   * independent candidates\nL112:   * candidates for unregistered parties and\nL113:   * candidates for registered parties not making a bulk nomination.\nL114: \nL115: You have to be nominated by two voters enrolled in the electorate you want to contest.\nL116: \nL117: A $300 deposit must be paid with an individual nomination.\nL118: Nominations can be lodged from Monday 7 September 2026. You can send your completed nomination to nominations@elections.govt.nz. The deadline to lodge your individual electorate candidate nomination is noon on Thursday 8 October 2026.\nL119: \nL120: cite44†Candidate nomination form - 2026 General Election pdf 309 KB L121: ### Bulk nomination of electorate candidates by registered parties\nL122: \nL123: Only registered parties can make a bulk nomination of electorate candidates. This is where the party secretary nominates all the electorate candidates representing the party by lodging a bulk nomination schedule with the Electoral Commission.\nL124: \nL125: Contact your party secretary if you are being bulk nominated to stand as an electorate candidate for the 2026 General Election.\nL126: Parties can lodge their bulk nomination of electorate candidates from Monday 7 September.\nL127: \nL128: The deadline to lodge a bulk nomination schedule for the 2026 General Election is noon on Thursday 8 October 2026.\nL129: ### Nominating list candidates\nL130: \nL131: Only registered parties can stand list candidates. Party list candidates are lodged with the Electoral Commission by the party secretary.\nL132: \nL133: Contact your party secretary if you are a list candidate for the 2026 General Election.\nL134: \nL135: Parties can lodge their party lists from Monday 7 September.\nL136: \nL137: The deadline to lodge a party list for the 2026 General Election is noon on Thursday 8 October 2026.\nL138: ### Release of candidate details\nL139: \nL140: We will publish candidate and party names (or independent) on cite45†vote.nz†vote.nz following the close of nominations. We do not publish any other candidate information.\nL141: \nL142: cite1†Back to top L143: \nL144: cite37†Party Portal Login cite5†About the Electoral Commission | cite6†Media & news | cite46†Privacy & security | cite7†Jobs†work.elections.nz | cite8†Contact L145: \nL146: 0800 36 76 56\nL147: cite47†Get in touch via our Facebook†www.facebook.com cite48†Follow us on Twitter†www.twitter.com cite49†Follow us on Instagram†www.instagram.com cite50†Have a look at our YouTube channel†www.youtube.com cite51†Connect with u