 L61: \nL62: cite23†Educating adults and communities L63: \nL64: cite24†How you can get more involved L65: cite25†Get brochures, posters and forms L66: \nL67: cite26†Download resources L68: \nL69: cite27†Candidate Hub L70: \nL71: cite28†Election Access Fund L72: \nL73: cite29†Community Education Fund L74: \nL75:   * Stats and research Ngā tatauranga me te rangahau\nL76: \nL77: cite30†Enrolment statistics L78: \nL79: cite31†Participation in voting L80: \nL81: cite32†Applications for roll data L82: \nL83: cite33†MMP seat allocation calculator L84: \nL85: cite34†Party donations and loans L86: \nL87: cite35†Election reports L88: \nL89: cite36†Election results†electionresults.govt.nz L90: \nL91: cite5†About us cite6†Media & news cite7†Jobs†work.elections.nz cite8†Contact L92: cite37†Party Portal Login L93: \nL94: [Button: In this section]\nL95: \nL96: cite10†Political parties in New Zealand L97: \nL98:   * Register of political parties\nL99:   * cite38†Current party and logo applications L100:   * cite39†Party donations and loans by year L101:   * cite40†Annual financial statements L102:   * cite41†Donations exceeding $20,000 L103:   * cite42†Party loans exceeding $30,000 L104:   * cite43†Donations protected from disclosure L105: If a political party wants to contest the party vote in an election, it must register with us. We keep a register of these parties and make it available to the public.\nL106: \nL107: The register shows each party’s:\nL108: \nL109:   * name\nL110:   * abbreviated name\nL111:   * component parties, if it has any\nL112:   * registration date\nL113:   * registration date of current logo\nL114:   * deadline for filing financial statements and whether these must be audited\nL115:   * secretary and their contact information\nL116:   * party rules.\nL117: A party with a registered abbreviation can either have their full party name or their abbreviated party name on the ballot paper. Where a party uses their abbreviated party name on the ballot paper this is noted in the register. All other parties use their full name on the ballot paper.\nL118: \nL119: You can download the register at the bottom of this page.\nL120: \nL121: cite39†See each party’s donation returns by year L122: ## Table of registered parties\nL123: \nL124: This table shows which parties are on the register, their abbreviated names, their registered logos, and links to their websites.\nL125: \nL126: * * *\nL127: \nL128: ## ACT New Zealand\nL129: \nL130: ### Party registered:\nL131: \nL132: 17 February 1995\nL133: \nL134: ### Component parties:\nL135: \nL136: None\nL137: \nL138: ### Abbreviation:\nL139: \nL140: The ACT Party\nL141: \nL142: ### Registered logo:\nL143: \nL144: cite44†Image: The ACT Party logo August 2019 L145: \nL146: ### Logo registered:\nL147: \nL148: 2 August 2019\nL149: \nL150: ### Party rules:\nL151: \nL152: cite45†The ACT Party - Constitution and Rules L153: ### Party secretary name and contact details:\nL154: \nL155: Callum Purves\nL156: Party Secretary\nL157: ACT New Zealand\nL158: PO Box 99651\nL159: Newmarket\nL160: Auckland 1149\nL161: \nL162: Ph: 027 330 2207\nL163: Email: callum.purves@act.org.nz\nL164: \nL165: ### Deadline for providing financial statements:\nL166: \nL167: 30 June\nL168: \nL169: ### Audit requirement for financial statements:\nL170: \nL171: Financial statements are not required to be audited\nL172: \nL173: ### Website:\nL174: \nL175: cite46†www.act.org.nz†www.act.org.nz L176: ### Previous registered logos:\nL177: \nL178: cite47†Image: The ACT Party logo September 2016 Registered: 30 Sep 2016\nL179: \nL180: cite48†Image: The ACT Party logo April 2014 Registered: 29 Apr 2014\nL181: \nL182: cite49†Image: The ACT Party logo August 2010 Registered: 25 Aug 2010\nL183: \nL184: cite50†Image: The ACT Party logo June 2003 Registered: 13 Jun 2003\nL185: \nL186: cite51†Image: The ACT Party logo May 1996 Registere